      "content": "1. Background: Why Europeans Came to India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Portuguese were the first Europeans to arrive in India (1498) and the last to leave (1961).",
        "The English East India Company was formed in 1600 under a Royal Charter from Queen Elizabeth I.",
        "Dutch trade shifted focus primarily to the spice islands of Indonesia after conflicts with the British.",
        "The Anglo-French rivalry in South India led to three Carnatic Wars, ultimately establishing British supremacy."
